exports[`guideToMarkdown > matches the snapshot for the fixture 1`] = `
"# Example Notes: OAuth app guide

**Tier 2: Self-serve, optional review.** Any user can connect as soon as you register. Review only matters if you want a directory listing.

**Next step:** Create a public integration in the Example Notes developer portal.

Confidence: medium. Researched 2026-10-28. Live, not verified. Source: https://example.org/guides/example-notes-mock01

## Start today

Composio-managed OAuth: unknown. This is a fictional app, so there is no Composio toolkit for it.

## Time and effort

| Stage | Who can connect | Hands-on | Waiting | Review |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Prototype | You and anyone you share the link with. | 15 min to 30 min | none | no |
| Production | Any user. | 1 h to 3 h | Provider says 0 to 7 days; developers report 0 to 14 days | no |

## Scopes

| Scope tier | Example scopes | Review | Serves | Effect |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Read pages | \`pages:read\` | No review | Read data | No review. Works for any user right away. |
| Edit pages | \`pages:write\` | No review | Write data, Act while offline | No review. Refresh tokens are issued by default. |
| Workspace admin | \`workspace:admin\` | Light review | Admin-level | A short form review before admin scopes work outside your own workspace. |

## Requirements

- [ ] An Example Notes account (prototype)
- [ ] A privacy policy URL (production): Needed only for a directory listing.

## Steps

- [ ] **Create a public integration** (you, 10 min, prototype). Open the developer portal, choose New integration, pick Public, and add your redirect URI. https://example.com/developers
- [ ] **Paste the client ID and secret into your auth config** (you, 5 min, prototype). Copy both values from the integration page into your Composio auth config or secret store.
- [ ] **Draft the directory listing text** (agent, 5 min, production). Use the app description draft below and edit it to match your product.
- [ ] **Wait for listing review** (provider, 0 to 14 days, production). Only if you applied for a listing. Your app keeps working for all users while you wait.

## Blockers

- **redirect_uri_mismatch on the consent screen.** Cause: The redirect URI in your request does not exactly match one registered on the integration. Fix: Copy the exact callback URL, including the trailing path, into the integration settings. Help: Example Notes developer forum

## Open questions

- **How long does listing review take in practice?** We found no developer reports. To resolve: Ask in the developer forum.

## Sources

1. [Example Notes OAuth docs](https://example.com/docs/oauth) (sourced, retrieved 2026-10-28)
2. <https://example.com/docs/listing> (sourced, retrieved 2026-10-28)
3. <https://example.com/oauth/authorize> (probed, retrieved 2026-10-28)
"
`;
